# --- .NET ---
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/
*.user
.vs/
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage

# The config file holds the static tokens and the SSH credentials, and §6.1 of
# HANDOFF.md requires it to be mode 0600 on disk. A copy of it in git is the
# same secret with the file mode removed, so the pattern is here rather than in
# a reviewer's head. `sshwarden.example.toml` is checked in on purpose and is
# excluded below - it carries placeholder values that the loader refuses.
sshwarden.toml
*.sshwarden.toml
!sshwarden.example.toml

# SSH private keys, whatever they get named locally.
*.pem
*.key
id_ed25519*
id_rsa*

# The audit log is the deployment's record of what ran on its own production
# hosts, including command output. It is the one artefact of this project that
# must never leave the machine that produced it.
*.jsonl
audit/

# The handoff brief, which is written to an agent rather than to a reader of this project - it
# names a person, their timezone and how they want to be talked to. Its design content lives in
# docs/DESIGN.md, in English, with the section numbers the code cites. Ignored so a working copy
# kept beside the repository cannot be committed by accident.
HANDOFF.md
